+# Complete public copy after compiler exit
+
+This is a build-process-only change. `npm run build` retains both data checks,
+then runs `scripts/build-deferred-public.mjs`. The official build helper already
+waits for that package script; its separate package helper is unchanged.
+
+1. Snapshot every physical `public` file and directory, including hidden files
+   and empty directories, with original size and SHA-256. Reject links/specials.
+2. Run the existing framework entry in a compiler child. Only that child's
+   environment receives `SITES_DEFER_PUBLIC_COPY=1`; the tracked Vite config then
+   sets `environments.client.build.copyPublicDir=false`. `publicDir` is unchanged.
+3. Wait for successful child exit, then start a separate small copy process.
+   Verify the complete public inventory again, require generated server/client
+   outputs, preflight every destination collision, and copy every original file
+   using `COPYFILE_EXCL`. Verify bytes/SHA after each copy and recheck the entire
+   source inventory. Do not transform, link, omit, prune, overwrite or upload.
+4. Only complete success writes `.sites-runtime/deferred-public-copy.json` with
+   the complete inventory and digest. This ignored local receipt is neither a
+   runtime asset nor independent live-upload evidence. Do not reuse a receipt
+   from an earlier attempt: require the current build's exit status and log.
+
+Direct framework builds without that private process-local flag retain their
+usual copy behavior. Dev/preview configuration is unchanged. Do not manually
+set the flag outside this wrapper. No dependency, installed helper, native
+image, UI, data, permission, source-public or pruning guard is changed.
+
+## Installed-source compatibility and limits
+
+Reviewed against Vite 8.0.13, vinext 1.0.0-beta.5, RSC plugin 0.5.26 and Cloudflare
+plugin 1.37.1. Their client configuration merges preserve this explicit option.
+Server public-route generation still scans the original source public tree.
+The current app has no prerender/export/standalone configuration; its successful
+A build has no prerender phase. Build postprocessing reads generated JS/CSS and
+manifests, not image bytes from dist/client. Reassess this ordering if adding
+prerender/export or a plugin that consumes copied public files during build.
+
+Generated `.assetsignore`, `_headers`, manifests and bundles are never replaced.
+A future source public path colliding with any generated file fails closed,
+even if the bytes match. No such conflict or public symlink was found in the
+current complete inventory: 1,806 files, 461,499,808 bytes.
+
+The hypothesis is reduced overlap between compiler heap/native memory and tmpfs
+pages used by the full public copy. Exit 137 alone did not establish an OOM
+cause. Source inspection and fixture tests do not prove a successful real build,
+peak-memory reduction, unchanged compiled chunk identities or deployability.
+The wrapper does not tune system resources or select a different environment.
+A controlled real build, fresh carrier-pin review, existing exact 194 plus the
+separate reviewed four-image pruning gates, and full expanded-tar measurement
+with at least 2 MiB headroom remain required. No pruning happens in this script.
+
+If compilation fails, copying never starts. If copying/disk verification fails,
+partial generated output may remain and the build fails; do not package it or
+automatically retry. Source files are read-only inputs. Only this attempt's
+owned generated intermediates may be cleaned under separate authorization.
+
+## Reproduction
+
+Focused fixtures, no full build or Vite/plugin initialization:
+`node --test tests/deferred-public-build.test.mjs`
+
+When separately authorized, use the unchanged official build helper through
+`bash scripts/sites-env.sh -- node <sites-helper>/scripts/build-site.mjs`.
+The new tracked package entry is sufficient; no temporary config edit/restore,
+public symlink, sparse deletion, hidden exclude list or helper modification.
